- [verified] DOCS VHOST BROKE HTTPS ON INSTALL; FIXED BY QUOTING THE REGEX: content install completed byte-identical and port 80 served it, but deploy.sh's nginx -t failed so the reload correctly never happened and HTTPS fell through to the default vhost. Cause: vhost line 63, an unquoted regex containing { } — nginx's lexer treats braces as structural even inside a regex. The defect was authored into the launch package and never test-loaded before production; until fixed, the on-disk global config was invalid, so any nginx restart would have taken every awsbox vhost down. Fix (quote the regex) validated in a copied-tree harness with a negative control reproducing the exact emerg; Will fixed the installed file himself in an editor.

